{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793472985,"nonce":"4zeN0OBqAzF2AZuyKoXbh9HJGuU=","title":"A compiled function called from the interpreter reads a garbage register for an omitted optional argument","message":"crates/ash_cli/tests/optional_dyn_call.rs aborted in a debug build in hybrid at --jit-threshold 1: \"misaligned pointer dereference: address must be a multiple of 0x8 but is 0xb\" at std/src/cast.rs:165, called from compiled String.indexOf, whose `?startIndex` (null\u003ci32\u003e) argument was omitted. Release builds passed because the register happened to hold zero.\n\nCause: the null padding for omitted optional arguments from 8287782b (git-bug d01c826) runs in the interpreter's own call path, after call_function has already dispatched to the compiled entry. call_compiled_entry marshalled only the arguments passed, so the compiled body read an unset argument register.\n\nFix: pad to the entry's arity with null inside call_compiled_entry when every omitted parameter accepts null. The existing test now passes in a debug build.","files":null}]}